  "scope": "Both released audit record projections over unchanged native SQLite row reads, command-or-principal-key selection, optional-row handling and native fault wrapping.",
  "limitations": [
    "Raw SQLite fixtures deliberately omit constraints to exercise row/type corruption. They are not valid checkpoints, saved-frame import or proof of cancellation authority.",
    "The frozen projection policy shares SQLite row reads, the unchanged command identity primitive and native fault formatter, not the migrated record/replay decoder. It is not an independent database implementation.",
    "Principal/session and raw replay token/key remain observations, not new admission checks. Matching, authorization and terminal cancellation evidence are enforced by their existing later owners.",
    "The 180 native lookup scenarios each compare both read and replay-query paths. SQL selection, transaction lifetime and missing-row semantics are intentionally unchanged.",
    "Existing cancellation commit, reopen and checkpoint recovery tests run in the related-crate regression; complete independent host-neutral durable recovery remains open.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, physical multi-host, power-loss or throughput benchmark is claimed."
